(242905, 13884, 6328, '<td valign="top">Numbers By The Hand Of God<br/>Greetings Vision,<br/>Critique by Silver Fox.<br/> <br/>When I first saw this, I assumed that it was supposed to be the number five, so when I saw your comments, I was glad that I was right for a change.<br/> <br/>You show some good imagination and originality for this Challenge, but Im not sure what to say about the composition as the Hand as you show it photographed seems a bit out of proportion.<br/> <br/>You show good focus on the Palm of the hand but as one looks forward towards the end of your baby and ring fingers, they seem to go out of focus.  Why?  Because of your enlargement of the photograph?  You also show excellent palmistry lineage from your sharp focus which shows good life and intuition lines.<br/> <br/>IMO, Visual interest of your photograph is due to the angle that you shot it and to the blue color of your ring and the green grass beneath your hand.<br/> <br/>All in all,  I think you scored kind of low, but all I can say is keep shooting, have fun, and I look forward to seeing more of your work next Challenge!<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Silver Fox<br/></td>', 'Numbers By The Hand Of GodGreetings Vision,Critique by Silver Fox. When I first saw this, I assumed that it was supposed to be the number five, so when I saw your comments, I was glad that I was right for a change. You show some good imagination and originality for this Challenge, but Im not sure what to say about the composition as the Hand as you show it photographed seems a bit out of proportion. You show good focus on the Palm of the hand but as one looks forward towards the end of your baby and ring fingers, they seem to go out of focus.  Why?  Because of your enlargement of the photograph?  You also show excellent palmistry lineage from your sharp focus which shows good life and intuition lines. IMO, Visual interest of your photograph is due to the angle that you shot it and to the blue color of your ring and the green grass beneath your hand. All in all,  I think you scored kind of low, but all I can say is keep shooting, have fun, and I look forward to seeing more of your work next Challenge! Regards,Silver Fox', '2003-03-21 20:00:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(242992, 13760, 3280, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club };-) </b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts </b> <br/>Beautiful shot, meets the challenge, may be a touch over exposed.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content </b> <br/>One of my favorites of the week.  A nice subtle natural number in High Key.  Composition is excellent as the cattails seem to sit just perfectly in the frame. Nice eye to find the number.<br/> <br/><b>Technical</b> <br/>Focus is excellent, especially with the light. The only thing I might have done was boost the contrast a little to make the plants stand out more against the snow. <br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo </b> <br/>I originally scored this shot a seven which was on the high end of your scores. I think that it meets the challenge well and was probably misunderstood by some of the voters as I feel it should have finished even higher than it did. Good job, and keep up the good work. <br/> <br/> <br/>I would be happy to talk further about this shot if you would like to contact me.<br/><b>DougPaz</b> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club };-)   Initial thoughts  Beautiful shot, meets the challenge, may be a touch over exposed. Composition/ Content  One of my favorites of the week.  A nice subtle natural number in High Key.  Composition is excellent as the cattails seem to sit just perfectly in the frame. Nice eye to find the number. Technical Focus is excellent, especially with the light. The only thing I might have done was boost the contrast a little to make the plants stand out more against the snow.  My Opinion On The Photo  I originally scored this shot a seven which was on the high end of your scores. I think that it meets the challenge well and was probably misunderstood by some of the voters as I feel it should have finished even higher than it did. Good job, and keep up the good work.   I would be happy to talk further about this shot if you would like to contact me.DougPaz ', '2003-03-22 00:12:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(242999, 13792, 1863, '<td valign="top">Welcome to the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>YAY! I''m so pleased to be critiqueing this photo, mainly because I LOOOOVE snails. Is this gravel and an aquatic snail? I''m not sure if there''s water there, but that''s definitely gravel. <br/> <br/>This to me is a very strong image, technically and.. on top of that, I find it very appealing in that I like snails. I can understand if others don''t find it so appealing, lol.. snails are a bit phobia for some people.<br/> <br/>The light in this photo is superb, it''s not too bright or to harsh, and it''s not too little. The shadow adds to the depth of the photo.<br/> <br/>Does it fit the challenge? You can''t get a more natural six, hehe. Beautiful photo, beautiful idea. Well done.<br/>-Da</td>', 'Welcome to the Critique Club: YAY! I''m so pleased to be critiqueing this photo, mainly because I LOOOOVE snails. Is this gravel and an aquatic snail? I''m not sure if there''s water there, but that''s definitely gravel.  This to me is a very strong image, technically and.. on top of that, I find it very appealing in that I like snails. I can understand if others don''t find it so appealing, lol.. snails are a bit phobia for some people. The light in this photo is superb, it''s not too bright or to harsh, and it''s not too little. The shadow adds to the depth of the photo. Does it fit the challenge? You can''t get a more natural six, hehe. Beautiful photo, beautiful idea. Well done.-Da', '2003-03-22 00:50:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(243042, 13795, 3599, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the nice comments everyone.  I decided not to title this with a number as there are a couple of different numbers in there so I left it to the viewer to decide.</td>', 'Thanks for all the nice comments everyone.  I decided not to title this with a number as there are a couple of different numbers in there so I left it to the viewer to decide.', '2003-03-22 05:11:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(243550, 13700, 527, '<td valign="top">Critique Club critique by Tim Jensen<br/> <br/>To be honest this appears to be a photo that was entered at the last moment when you didn''t have a better idea. I don''t mean to be harsh but I just don''t find this to be a very compelling photo. I feel it is borderline in meeting the challenge as well because you created the 1 shape yourself so it wasnt naturally occurring. But it''s probably close enough. If you had to use your own hand then I think you should have tried to create a semi-abstract, compositionally strong image. Strong, contrasty light and maybe the use of black and white would have created a more visually appealing photo. There is interesting texture in the wall and more could have been done with that with some strong sidelighting. I hope this helps. It''s all good practice and that is the main point of this site so I hope you can use this advice in a positive way. <br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'Critique Club critique by Tim Jensen To be honest this appears to be a photo that was entered at the last moment when you didn''t have a better idea. I don''t mean to be harsh but I just don''t find this to be a very compelling photo. I feel it is borderline in meeting the challenge as well because you created the 1 shape yourself so it wasnt naturally occurring. But it''s probably close enough. If you had to use your own hand then I think you should have tried to create a semi-abstract, compositionally strong image. Strong, contrasty light and maybe the use of black and white would have created a more visually appealing photo. There is interesting texture in the wall and more could have been done with that with some strong sidelighting. I hope this helps. It''s all good practice and that is the main point of this site so I hope you can use this advice in a positive way.  Tim', '2003-03-23 16:00:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(243701, 13758, 4493, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comment:<br/> <br/>This is a nice shot that shows the quiet morning hours. The dew on the ground is a nice element. I think that that other then the sky being a little bright and the darker areas not being deeper in their depth of shade you have a nice composition that meets the numbers requirement well. Your crop may have been a little tighter to crop out the black line in the lower right and doing a metering on the sky would have darkened up the ground elements giving them more depth.<br/> <br/>Nice shot!</td>', 'Critique Club Comment: This is a nice shot that shows the quiet morning hours. The dew on the ground is a nice element. I think that that other then the sky being a little bright and the darker areas not being deeper in their depth of shade you have a nice composition that meets the numbers requirement well. Your crop may have been a little tighter to crop out the black line in the lower right and doing a metering on the sky would have darkened up the ground elements giving them more depth. Nice shot!', '2003-03-23 20:04:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(243729, 13773, 4162, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition-Content<br/> <br/>You found an excellent subject for this challenge, well spotted! I agree with inspzil that perhaps positioning the circles in the bottom right corner would have added more interest composition wise.<br/> <br/>Technical<br/>Nice overall lighting here, which shows the texture well. My biggest point is that focus seems pretty soft here, I notice that you used a slow shutter speed, did you have a tripod? Texture of the wood is the main attraction of this shot and would benefit from being super sharp, either through afaster shutter speed or use of a tripod.<br/> <br/>My Opinion<br/>Great shot and wonderful textures. Excellent capture for the challenge.</td>', 'Critique Club Composition-Content You found an excellent subject for this challenge, well spotted! I agree with inspzil that perhaps positioning the circles in the bottom right corner would have added more interest composition wise. TechnicalNice overall lighting here, which shows the texture well. My biggest point is that focus seems pretty soft here, I notice that you used a slow shutter speed, did you have a tripod? Texture of the wood is the main attraction of this shot and would benefit from being super sharp, either through afaster shutter speed or use of a tripod. My OpinionGreat shot and wonderful textures. Excellent capture for the challenge.', '2003-03-23 21:08:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(243773, 13979, 4162, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition-Content<br/> <br/>This is a lovely picture, a really pretty scene. Perhaps the Natural Numbers are not as obvious as others, but as the picture stands, it is great! <br/> <br/>Technical<br/> <br/>DOF is perfect, great sharpness on the petals and a very attractive blurred background. The flowers really jump out! Lighting also enhances this effect, with the light falling on the petals and creating beautiful colours and contrast. The border complements the picture and colours very well.<br/> <br/>My Opinion<br/> <br/>This is a lovely shot, I think that the Natural Number element probably wasn''t strong enough for most voters, but this was a very hard challenge and I think that you did a great job!</td>', 'Critique Club Composition-Content This is a lovely picture, a really pretty scene. Perhaps the Natural Numbers are not as obvious as others, but as the picture stands, it is great!  Technical DOF is perfect, great sharpness on the petals and a very attractive blurred background. The flowers really jump out! Lighting also enhances this effect, with the light falling on the petals and creating beautiful colours and contrast. The border complements the picture and colours very well. My Opinion This is a lovely shot, I think that the Natural Number element probably wasn''t strong enough for most voters, but this was a very hard challenge and I think that you did a great job!', '2003-03-23 21:31:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(243851, 13672, 3280, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club };-) </b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts </b> <br/>Beautiful colors, kind of meets the challenge, nice in an abstract sort of way.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content </b> <br/>The colors are awesome but as I looked at it originally it appeared to be a sky shot turned sideways.  In my mind that qualified more as an "equal sign" than an eleven. I''m afraid that your score indicates that most of the voters felt something similar. A beatiful shot but perhaps not a good scorer in this challenge. <br/> <br/><b>Technical</b> <br/>The shot appears a bit grainey but it was probably in relatively low light. It''s hard to tell if you saturated it like this in post-processing or these are original colors but they are stunning. A little horizon in the forefront probably would make this a better sunset shot but would ruin your Challenge shot!<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo </b> <br/>I originally scored this shot a four as did most of the voters. I think that it''s very pretty but is a stretch to meet the challenge. Good job anyway, I generally appreciate your use of color and composition.  I like the fact that you are not afraid to try something new even if it may not score well!  Way to go and keep up the good work. <br/> <br/> <br/>I would be happy to talk further about this shot if you would like to contact me.<br/><b>DougPaz</b> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club };-)   Initial thoughts  Beautiful colors, kind of meets the challenge, nice in an abstract sort of way. Composition/ Content  The colors are awesome but as I looked at it originally it appeared to be a sky shot turned sideways.  In my mind that qualified more as an "equal sign" than an eleven. I''m afraid that your score indicates that most of the voters felt something similar. A beatiful shot but perhaps not a good scorer in this challenge.  Technical The shot appears a bit grainey but it was probably in relatively low light. It''s hard to tell if you saturated it like this in post-processing or these are original colors but they are stunning. A little horizon in the forefront probably would make this a better sunset shot but would ruin your Challenge shot! My Opinion On The Photo  I originally scored this shot a four as did most of the voters. I think that it''s very pretty but is a stretch to meet the challenge. Good job anyway, I generally appreciate your use of color and composition.  I like the fact that you are not afraid to try something new even if it may not score well!  Way to go and keep up the good work.   I would be happy to talk further about this shot if you would like to contact me.DougPaz ', '2003-03-23 22:58:41.000000', NULL, 0),
